In article <1994Jan2.203536.3125@cc.ic.ac.uk>, arbh@chcmgb.NoSubdomain.NoDomain (Mr A.R.B. Hashim) writes:
>How best to deal with the wizard? If you tin his corpse
>will it stop him from coming back. How about eating it?
>

Tinning his corpse won't help.
Eating it won't help.

Although I haven't had these work with 3.1 (aside from in wizard mode)
I understand there are a few ways to get rid of him forever.  Some 
people have said that they won't work anymore, but as far as I know
they still seem to.

The traditional approach is to throw a potion of paralysis at him and 
then go up the up stairs before he recovers.  Since time doesn't pass 
when you're not on a level, he's stuck there paralyzed forever.  And 
no new wiz's will be created since there's already one who exists
somewhere.

Another way I thought of was to use the fact that the wiz teleports to
the upstairs to recover when he's hurt.  If you let him do that in Vlad's
tower, and then go down, you can continue back in the main dungeon, and
never meet him again.  Someone else suggested quaffing a cursed potion of
gain level while he's recovering on the upstairs, but I've never tried
that.

>Whats the best way to resist the curses from eg Lichs?
>Does stormbringer resist curses? A few times I had the mesage
>"stormbriger resists!" What does it mean?

Genocide the genocidable ones (like liches), and kill the rest as soon 
as you see them.  Keep a few backup potions of holy water, and maybe
a blessed scroll of remove curse in a sack (not a Bag of holding).  
Also put your bag of holding inside a sack (not another Bag of holding).

Some intelligent artifacts, like Stormbringer and Excalibur resist curses.
